{"title":"2005 AIME II Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:50%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II\" title=\"2005 AIME II\">2005 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b>)<br /> <span class=\"noprint plainlinks\"> <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=2005\">AoPS Contest Collections</a> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/contest/download/c3416/2005\">PDF</a>\n</span></td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"font-size:80%;\">\n<p><font style=\"text-align:center;\">Instructions</font>\n</p>\n<ol><li>This is a 15-question, 3-hour examination. All answers are integers ranging from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/7/dc7ddbca9440579298bf24e0f9bcf2c0457bfc1b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$000$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/7/0/0705411d92671faf1fe5602cfef8f353c7f0f83d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$999$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />, inclusive. Your score will be the number of correct answers; i.e., there is neither partial credit nor a penalty for wrong answers.</li>\n<li>No aids other than scratch paper, rulers and compasses are permitted. In particular, <u><b>graph paper, protractors, calculators and computers are not permitted.</b></u></li></ol>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">15</a>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#Problem_11\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 11</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-12\"><a href=\"#Problem_12\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">12</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 12</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-13\"><a href=\"#Problem_13\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">13</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 13</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-14\"><a href=\"#Problem_14\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">14</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 14</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-15\"><a href=\"#Problem_15\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">15</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 15</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-16\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">16</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A game uses a deck of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> different cards, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is an integer and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/3/9e379c6fee7b1248e81a4e5882f92066a79517aa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n \\geq 6.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"47\" height=\"15\" /> The number of possible sets of 6 cards that can be drawn from the deck is 6 times the number of possible sets of 3 cards that can be drawn. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/d/9/bd923e41635af40a1abe58f230732f2280b0723a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A hotel packed breakfast for each of three guests. Each breakfast should have consisted of three types of rolls, one each of nut, cheese, and fruit rolls. The preparer wrapped each of the nine rolls and once wrapped, the rolls were indistinguishable from one another. She then randomly put three rolls in a bag for each of the guests. Given that the probability each guest got one roll of each type is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/0/3d01476c4fc8b19ad9eb851ff22a83a669363212.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac mn,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"24\" height=\"33\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime integers, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db26f75f6218a382840f0ed34f5d36bcff61d33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An infinite geometric series has sum 2005. A new series, obtained by squaring each term of the original series, has 10 times the sum of the original series. The common ratio of the original series is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/b/9/9b9ffa9646e74f6e94a4a66b824c3a3f08f4f4b9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac mn$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"18\" height=\"33\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime integers. Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db26f75f6218a382840f0ed34f5d36bcff61d33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find the number of positive integers that are divisors of at least one of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/1/6/116f0b7c1f34a5fa42adbe97a21f68882e12c7b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10^{10},15^7,18^{11}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"110\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Determine the number of ordered pairs <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/8/8e8da0aef2d19017da7471378386d61620f288f5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(a,b)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> of integers such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/6/ec681752d07cf39ef247a45331d818a6a96b8738.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\log_a b + 6\\log_b a=5, 2 \\leq a \\leq 2005,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"268\" height=\"17\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/7/4a7281beebcb361c170844771b8c1d4e708fa6d3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\leq b \\leq 2005.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"105\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The cards in a stack of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f93f5c51ea4b04b4992b003b39479f29018f6bda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> cards are numbered consecutively from 1 through <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/3/f93f5c51ea4b04b4992b003b39479f29018f6bda.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2n$\" width=\"19\" height=\"12\" /> from top to bottom. The top <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> cards are removed, kept in order, and form pile <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/2/0/8207b79435a4bd499da7598fb44424c8a8499238.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" /> The remaining cards form pile <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/9/5/b95fbfb49b675ba11392ba7c2603d0c87f89be76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"22\" height=\"14\" /> The cards are then restacked by taking cards alternately from the tops of pile <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/1/0c1e22fe09c7388d738ebd1e52fb999e0eae620f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> respectively. In this process, card number <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/c/99cb3f3a8b3bbfc702c5863d16602a06cded535d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(n+1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"54\" height=\"18\" /> becomes the bottom card of the new stack, card number 1 is on top of this card, and so on, until piles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> are exhausted. If, after the restacking process, at least one card from each pile occupies the same position that it occupied in the original stack, the stack is named magical. Find the number of cards in the magical stack in which card number 131 retains its original position.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/7/6f71d4755273a86295f916ae662a281e75af55c6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=\\frac{4}{(\\sqrt{5}+1)(\\sqrt[4]{5}+1)(\\sqrt[8]{5}+1)(\\sqrt[16]{5}+1)}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -19px\" width=\"328\" height=\"43\" /> Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/5/6f5b2ce1d3747ada30454afa2318e53f817d4c01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x+1)^{48}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"73\" height=\"19\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 7\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70b97eb4ad6e4e7a5a97e2547d9ed6e965960d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/5/b65e6facfe122c182fe14d503aeace2c52a9739d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> are externally tangent, and they are both internally tangent to circle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/9/c/99c2c622c15fb0f79a77bbee386885bfc7ad80db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_3.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"24\" height=\"15\" /> The radii of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70b97eb4ad6e4e7a5a97e2547d9ed6e965960d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" />  and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/6/5/b65e6facfe122c182fe14d503aeace2c52a9739d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> are 4 and 10, respectively, and the centers of the three circles are all collinear. A chord of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/1/85160260d550bf33be28c0a722237c3bc60e8c02.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"15\" /> is also a common external tangent of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/0/b/70b97eb4ad6e4e7a5a97e2547d9ed6e965960d0c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"15\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/b/47b97f75ff19cf530ab5d58805c081503fb6b0e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C_2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"17\" /> Given that the length of the chord is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/b/b/fbb8849907f0cc454e885c12082ed11fc4fca671.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{m\\sqrt{n}}p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"44\" height=\"42\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/c/e/2ceed1f5c723a6e397dd8aa9fb1cfb894e1f6a91.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m,n,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"39\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are positive integers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are relatively prime, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is not divisible by the square of any prime, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/337be2d56c71c93d817fc635421ea2154bf992ae.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n+p.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"84\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 8\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>For how many positive integers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> less than or equal to 1000 is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/3/f53c3302151c8bc9e98ed3dc304935aded998ede.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\sin t + i \\cos t)^n = \\sin nt + i \\cos nt$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"263\" height=\"18\" /> true for all real <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/d/e0d2bf360290fd61d1c1557e763f2622363b3d35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$t$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"8\" height=\"13\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 9\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is a regular octahedron, that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is the cube whose vertices are the centers of the faces of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/b/56b4c0ef575d9ec02ec52379f2cc6f6fa28acc13.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"16\" /> and that the ratio of the volume of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> to that of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/0/3d01476c4fc8b19ad9eb851ff22a83a669363212.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac mn,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"24\" height=\"33\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> are relatively prime integers, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/b/5db26f75f6218a382840f0ed34f5d36bcff61d33.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m+n.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"56\" height=\"14\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 10\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_11\">Problem 11</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 11\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> be a positive integer, and let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/3/783397ac918b3ab6b151f45e1dc2a903e6afe296.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0, a_1,\\ldots,a_m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"103\" height=\"11\" /> be a sequence of reals such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/3/2039cef08f76452b06bb58532edd04c587d5c703.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_0 = 37, a_1 = 72, a_m = 0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"194\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/8/408bd5f82b84326fd762a03bb386a36e640cac86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a_{k+1} = a_{k-1} - \\frac 3{a_k}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"136\" height=\"40\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/e/5fe4a9a7e9fddda77130f1dafacaab76f8ebff84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k = 1,2,\\ldots, m-1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"151\" height=\"16\" /> Find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/9/269981c02d6475e9e4ac1869e1b063ef377c2847.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m.$\" width=\"19\" height=\"8\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 11\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_12\">Problem 12</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=12\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 12\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Square <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/e/f9efaf9474c5658c4089523e2aff4e11488f8603.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCD$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"60\" height=\"14\" /> has center <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/4/e0407857e5e04f3c5647d95ebabe2ed4880d1ceb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O, AB=900, E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"124\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/5/a055f405829e64a3b70253ab67cb45ed6ed5bb29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/8/198b4925e89b7b9e2374130f3572b96458efc366.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE&lt;BF$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"81\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/b/93b63f87ebd2f9a55c43118284c161a14fbca81a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$F, m\\angle EOF =45^\\circ,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"146\" height=\"16\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/c/6bc116d2dbfa1566b044c719433d773084582806.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EF=400.$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"83\" height=\"13\" /> Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/9/7a91943541b0a22a717e074cd465d8986aa45f62.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BF=p+q\\sqrt{r},$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"121\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/6/9c6fa61e71277c83449530b062cbb563761d9ff2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p,q,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"31\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> are positive integers and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> is not divisible by the square of any prime, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/8/6/a86bc509d066a186211fd96c0f6e1487d69dda42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q+r.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"77\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 12\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_13\">Problem 13</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=13\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 13\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/f/6efaaf74e576202fad965134bc49c6a34aac4c30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(x)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"41\" height=\"20\" /> be a polynomial with integer coefficients that satisfies <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/e/c/6ec2c566436bfca6f74ea5b134227f79285e144a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(17)=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"88\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/7/207930a30a108a40220f0f3b3652c5e0d34dbd4a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(24)=17.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"92\" height=\"18\" /> Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/5/d154262ea1037809ed3ac135cd35175975b4fabd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P(n)=n+3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"105\" height=\"18\" /> has two distinct integer solutions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/f/defbf06b987965438e5928b96688e48df84cba0e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"16\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/a/b1a4ecf12066e05720578b74819681fb175bbf64.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_2,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"22\" height=\"11\" /> find the product <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/f/a/5fa2b0a76d3ff55c1a76ab95778995e974524821.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n_1\\cdot n_2.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"53\" height=\"10\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 13\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_14\">Problem 14</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=14\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 14\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/b/2/1b247c5fbdbcc90127b0611d1a5eb4463914bccf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC, AB=13, BC=15,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"207\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/c/3/fc3352a763097c23178aa1a48443089675b1aa9a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CA = 14.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"77\" height=\"14\" /> Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/d/e8db92d03b62e8cfafc8f05f30257af153a71d06.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$CD=6.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"70\" height=\"14\" /> Point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/2/fa2fa899f0afb05d6837885523503a2d4df434f9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is on <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/3/e33fe7d65facd8868f58b6e94ddc7f153a5a3f9f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> such that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/4/b1423845c6cd6b222174f1ab490f1923b02f94c0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BAE\\cong \\angle CAD.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"143\" height=\"15\" /> Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/5/4152b2a66492983b24a45d4d260282864ac5201e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BE=\\frac pq$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"68\" height=\"38\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are relatively prime positive integers, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/f/9cf560f497c604f9cdc8256b4352f8d49b0a43f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"16\" height=\"13\" />\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_14\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 14\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_15\">Problem 15</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=15\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 15\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/c/3/3c352e9db5a7134ca93f9fecce8fe99b0d4e5889.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w_1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/e/0ce0501dff8a93818a4e5d9ecc570d8ab6472e5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"10\" /> denote the circles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/a/beae495d446ffbc169bfd85bc96a5b60dfa6e7ba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2+y^2+10x-24y-87=0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"231\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/b/05b6f58c7c2befac6afa117a621ccc005d913e85.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x^2 +y^2-10x-24y+153=0,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"244\" height=\"18\" /> respectively. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/5/0/f5047d1e0cbb50ec208923a22cd517c55100fa7b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"10\" /> be the smallest positive value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> for which the line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/e/0/ee0459893b6e7c554d5a0d3ba8a3ce7ecb3cc0b8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y=ax$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"53\" height=\"11\" /> contains the center of a circle that is externally tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/e/0ce0501dff8a93818a4e5d9ecc570d8ab6472e5b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w_2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"19\" height=\"10\" /> and internally tangent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/e/d/9edffb65227019766dd92629f42296864cf9a209.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$w_1.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"24\" height=\"10\" /> Given that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/e/c/0ecc8c0ca82daa75ba3c4317e9f79352b9ca70de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$m^2=\\frac pq,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -16px\" width=\"65\" height=\"36\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/1/0615acc3725de21025457e7d6f7694dab8e2f758.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> are relatively prime integers, find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/3/043f651be7ed631a58104b324d1aa6c6c843beba.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p+q.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> \n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2005 AIME II Problems/Problem 15\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=16\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II\" title=\"2005 AIME II\">2005 AIME II</a></b> (<b><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_AIME_II_Answer_Key\" title=\"2005 AIME II Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum